u}$) and wavelength ($\lambda$) is given by:<br>$\lambda = \dfrac{1}{ ar{
u}}$<br><br>Given $ ar{
u} = 40000 \mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$, we have:<br>$\lambda = \dfrac{1}{40000} \mathrm{~cm} = 2.5 	imes 10^{-5} \mathrm{~cm}$<br><br>To convert centimeters to nanometers, we use the conversion factors $1 \mathrm{~cm} = 10^{-2} \mathrm{~m}$ and $1 \mathrm{~nm} = 10^{-9} \mathrm{~m}$:<br>$\lambda = 2.5 	imes 10^{-5} 	imes 10^{-2} \mathrm{~m} = 2.5 	imes 10^{-7} \mathrm{~m}$<br><br>$\lambda = \dfrac{2.5 	imes 10^{-7}}{10^{-9}} \mathrm{~nm} = 250 \mathrm{~nm}$<br><br>Answer: $250$

